> 1) what items should I leave behind initially, and

Inventory management is a major lesson in the game and how
to do it depends too much on your playing style to be able
to answer properly.

Keep items that are usefull and light, drop the ones that are
heavy and useless.  What is which is a judgement call.  For
example rocks are fine as missiles but how many or few to carry.

Generally I try on armor that is know to be not cursed and
drop any that is not better than my current, but I put it in a
pile near the stairs.  That leaves a *lot* of armor I am not
sure of its b/u/c status yet that gets left in a pile to be tested
eventually.

Weapons follow a similar pattern but missiles get carried
longer than mostly-melee ones.  Other items I need to know
it's use before I keep it in my inventory.

> 2) what's a safe way to
> leave things behind so that other creatures won't take them?

How safe is safe?

Be aggressive and leave them in stacks near the down stairs.
Be medium and leave them in containers.  Be paranoid and
put the e-word under the containers.



